{"resource":{"id":"computer-networks-pdf-notes","title":"Computer Networks — PDF Notes","category":"CS Core","difficulty":"Beginner","readingTime":"73 min","pages":86,"lastUpdated":"May 2026","tags":["Networks","TCP/IP","CS Core"],"heroImage":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1544197150-b99a580bb7a8?w=1800&q=80","heroSubtitle":"Chapter-wise Computer Networks notes: fundamentals, OSI, TCP/IP, IP addressing, subnetting, routing, switching, DNS, DHCP, HTTP, HTTPS, TCP, UDP, IPv6, NAT, VPN, firewalls, wireless, cloud, troubleshooting."},"toc":[{"id":"objectives","label":"Learning Objectives"},{"id":"intro","label":"Introduction"},{"id":"ch1","label":"Chapter 1 — Fundamentals"},{"id":"ch2","label":"Chapter 2 — OSI Model"},{"id":"ch3","label":"Chapter 3 — TCP/IP Model"},{"id":"ch4","label":"Chapter 4 — IP Addressing"},{"id":"ch5","label":"Chapter 5 — Subnetting"},{"id":"ch6","label":"Chapter 6 — Routing"},{"id":"ch7","label":"Chapter 7 — Switching & VLANs"},{"id":"ch8","label":"Chapter 8 — DNS & DHCP"},{"id":"ch9","label":"Chapter 9 — HTTP/HTTPS"},{"id":"ch10","label":"Chapter 10 — TCP & UDP"},{"id":"ch11","label":"Chapter 11 — IPv6"},{"id":"ch12","label":"Chapter 12 — NAT & VPN"},{"id":"ch13","label":"Chapter 13 — Firewalls & Security"},{"id":"ch14","label":"Chapter 14 — Wireless & Cloud"},{"id":"ch15","label":"Chapter 15 — Troubleshooting"},{"id":"compare","label":"Comparison Table"},{"id":"commands","label":"Commands & Code Reference"},{"id":"best","label":"Best Practices & Tips"},{"id":"mistakes","label":"Common Mistakes"},{"id":"summary","label":"Summary & Key Takeaways"},{"id":"faqs","label":"FAQs"},{"id":"references","label":"Further Reading & References"},{"id":"disclaimer","label":"Disclaimer"}],"related":[{"title":"Computer Networks — Complete Tutorial","tag":"CS Core","time":"47 min"},{"title":"Computer Networks — Cheat Sheet","tag":"CS Core","time":"5 min"},{"title":"Computer Networks — Interview Questions","tag":"CS Core","time":"43 min"}],"html":"<section id=\"objectives\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Learning Objectives</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li>Master the core ideas covered in this resource.</li>\n          <li>Apply concepts to hands-on labs and real networks.</li>\n          <li>Ready you for interviews and certifications.</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"intro\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Introduction</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Chapter-wise Computer Networks notes: fundamentals, OSI, TCP/IP, IP addressing, subnetting, routing, switching, DNS, DHCP, HTTP, HTTPS, TCP, UDP, IPv6, NAT, VPN, firewalls, wireless, cloud, troubleshooting.</p>\n        <Figure src=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1544197150-b99a580bb7a8?w=1400&q=80\" caption=\"Figure 1 — Overview illustration for Computer Networks — PDF Notes.\" />\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"ch1\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Chapter 1 — Fundamentals</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Networks, topologies, LAN/WAN/MAN, bandwidth, throughput, latency.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"ch2\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Chapter 2 — OSI Model</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Seven layers with PDUs, protocols, and devices at each.</p>\n        <Figure src=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1544197150-b99a580bb7a8?w=1400&q=80\" caption=\"Figure 1 — Reference diagram for chapter 2 — osi model.\" />\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"ch3\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Chapter 3 — TCP/IP Model</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Four-layer practical stack aligned to real-world protocols.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"ch4\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Chapter 4 — IP Addressing</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>IPv4 structure, classes, private ranges, ARP.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"ch5\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Chapter 5 — Subnetting</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Masks, CIDR, VLSM, aggregation. Practice drills.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"ch6\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Chapter 6 — Routing</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Static, dynamic, distance vector, link state, OSPF, BGP.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"ch7\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Chapter 7 — Switching &amp; VLANs</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>MAC learning, STP, trunking, 802.1Q, inter-VLAN routing.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"ch8\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Chapter 8 — DNS &amp; DHCP</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Record types, resolution flow, DHCP lease process.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"ch9\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Chapter 9 — HTTP/HTTPS</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Methods, status codes, TLS 1.3 handshake, HSTS.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"ch10\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Chapter 10 — TCP &amp; UDP</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Handshake, flow control, congestion control, common ports.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"ch11\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Chapter 11 — IPv6</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Address types, SLAAC, transition to IPv6.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"ch12\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Chapter 12 — NAT &amp; VPN</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>NAT variants, IPsec, SSL VPN.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"ch13\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Chapter 13 — Firewalls &amp; Security</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Stateful, NGFW, IDS/IPS, Zero Trust.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"ch14\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Chapter 14 — Wireless &amp; Cloud</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Wi-Fi standards, VPCs, hybrid connectivity.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"ch15\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Chapter 15 — Troubleshooting</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Layered approach, common tools, real scenarios.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"compare\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Comparison Table</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <table class=\"w-full border-collapse text-sm\">\n          <thead><tr><th class=\"border p-2 text-left\">Aspect</th><th class=\"border p-2 text-left\">TCP</th><th class=\"border p-2 text-left\">UDP</th></tr></thead>\n          <tbody>\n            <tr><td class=\"border p-2\">Reliability</td><td class=\"border p-2\">Guaranteed</td><td class=\"border p-2\">Best-effort</td></tr>\n            <tr><td class=\"border p-2\">Ordering</td><td class=\"border p-2\">Yes</td><td class=\"border p-2\">No</td></tr>\n            <tr><td class=\"border p-2\">Overhead</td><td class=\"border p-2\">Higher</td><td class=\"border p-2\">Lower</td></tr>\n            <tr><td class=\"border p-2\">Use cases</td><td class=\"border p-2\">HTTP, SSH, email</td><td class=\"border p-2\">DNS, VoIP, gaming</td></tr>\n          </tbody>\n        </table>\n        <Figure src=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1518770660439-4636190af475?w=1400&q=80\" caption=\"Figure 2 — Protocol behavior at a glance.\" />\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"commands\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Commands &amp; Code Reference</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>code</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>! Cisco IOS — VLAN + trunk basics\nvlan 10\n name USERS\nvlan 20\n name VOICE\ninterface GigabitEthernet0/1\n switchport mode access\n switchport access vlan 10\ninterface GigabitEthernet0/24\n switchport mode trunk\n switchport trunk allowed vlan 10,20</code></pre></div>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"best\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Best Practices &amp; Tips</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li>Baseline before you optimize.</li>\n          <li>Document intent, not just configs.</li>\n          <li>Automate repetitive changes.</li>\n          <li>Segment aggressively; deny by default.</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"mistakes\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Common Mistakes</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li>Overlapping subnets across sites.</li>\n          <li>Trunks allowing all VLANs.</li>\n          <li>Skipping change reviews.</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"summary\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Summary &amp; Key Takeaways</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Layered thinking, clean IP planning, and disciplined operations turn a network from fragile to boring — in the best way.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"faqs\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">FAQs</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <details class=\"group my-2 rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-card p-4 open:shadow-sm\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 text-sm font-semibold\"><span>How is this different from a general IT course?</span><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition group-open:rotate-90\"><path d=\"m9 18 6-6-6-6\"/></svg></summary><div class=\"mt-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground\">This resource focuses purely on networking concepts and their application.</div></details>\n        <details class=\"group my-2 rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-card p-4 open:shadow-sm\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 text-sm font-semibold\"><span>Do I need Cisco hardware?</span><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition group-open:rotate-90\"><path d=\"m9 18 6-6-6-6\"/></svg></summary><div class=\"mt-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground\">No — Packet Tracer and GNS3 emulate everything you need.</div></details>\n        <details class=\"group my-2 rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-card p-4 open:shadow-sm\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 text-sm font-semibold\"><span>Is content current?</span><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition group-open:rotate-90\"><path d=\"m9 18 6-6-6-6\"/></svg></summary><div class=\"mt-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground\">Yes — reflects modern protocols and enterprise practices as of May 2026.</div></details>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"references\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Further Reading &amp; References</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\"><References /></div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"disclaimer\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Disclaimer</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p class=\"text-sm text-muted-foreground\">Educational content. Vendor commands and versions may change — always verify against current documentation.</p>\n      </div></section>"}